web_agent里面的 _do_expand里面的 page.sections：{'full_text': 'James Madison Dates In Office: March 04, 1809 to March 04, 1817 Age in Office: 57 Birth - Death: March 16, 1751 to June 28, 1836 Party: Democratic-Republican Location Born: Virginia Office: Secretary of State Religion: Episcopalian More Resources JAMES MADISON EVENT TIMELINE FIRST LADY DOLLEY MADISON MADISON PRESIDENTIAL SITES AND ORGANIZATIONS: James Madison Presidential Papers (Library of Congress) James Madison Birthplace - Belle Grove Plantation, King George, VA James Madison Family Plantation - Montpelier Montpelier National Historical Landmark (NPS), Montpelier Station, VA The James Madison Museum of Orange County Heritage James Madison Memorial Building, Washington, DC BIOGRAPHIES OF JAMES MADISON Biography of James Madison by J.C.A. Stagg Biography of James Madison by Irving Brant Related Documents Search all documents March 02, 1809 Letter From the President Elect March 04, 1809 Inaugural Address March 04, 1809 James Madison Event Timeline April 19, 1809 Proclamation—Suspension of Prohibition of Trade Between the United States and Great Britain May 23, 1809 Special Session Message May 26, 1809 Special Message June 04, 1809 Special Message June 15, 1809 Special Message June 20, 1809 Special Message June 26, 1809 Special Message August 09, 1809 Proclamation—Renewal of Prohibition of Trade Between the United States and Great Britain November 29, 1809 First Annual Message December 12, 1809 Special Message December 16, 1809 Special Message December 16, 1809 Special Message December 22, 1809 Special Message January 03, 1810 Special Message January 09, 1810 Special Message January 15, 1810 Special Message January 22, 1810 Special Message February 28, 1810 Special Message March 15, 1810 Special Message March 27, 1810 Special Message May 28, 1810 Order—Authorization to Borrow Funds October 27, 1810 Proclamation 16—Taking Possession of Part of Louisiana (Annexation of West Florida) November 02, 1810 Proclamation